    "4:ב": "(2) (ב) (j) There are prohibitions - since Dain Ma'alan in sanctification AJG Dain Moridan GAC and indeed in all things that can be brought up in sanctity and the above but in the SAT that one cannot raise the blood in sanctity any more to the GAC when a sale is taken in a different image:",
    "4:ג": "(3) (ג) And there is a reason - since the Gemara does not remove them from their sanctity, etc. For the sake of retroactivity, but for the sake of the beginning, of course it is forbidden to sell anything sacred in order to take it, as it comes out of it, and even such a thing is delikha as an illustration of a crime, such as the other sacred thing is ready before us and there is nothing missing except the giving of the Apha, it is forbidden to bring it up with the sanctity. To begin with, he sold it in order to take another [Peri Megadim and Shaa]. The text of the siman 16 in our time we see many people selling books and taking others in their blood. It seems that now it begins when the buyer of the book was of the opinion that he would have twenty-seven that he would need, and if he had a better opportunity, he would sell it and take the beautiful one, even though he did not condition it in the interpretation, and the Rabbi wrote that the taste of the custom is because it is based on what is written in the siman 19 on its 10th, it is permissible to sell, etc.",
    "5:א": "(1) (א) Or Sat - Amma Damsayim no mshinin kai or danktiya for the name of the people who dammshin it for providing students and as dalkamiya in the S.O.:",
    "5:ב": "(2) (ב) There is no interpretation, etc. - and if the collectors want to lend them and then give others under them to the HMA, it is forbidden for the owners to give it to the person performing the mitzvah with this money precisely and for the 16th of the year, but by the seven good people of the city in the position of the people of the city for the siman 19, they sang to change the Ma'ot as in siman 7:",
    "5:ג": "(3) (ג) (Yid) For whatever they want - we were even something that has no sanctity at all, except that it is an accumulated need and the taste, since the opinion of the people of the city was made in the expression of the Shari Shari Bahamutar:",
    "5:ד": "(4) (ד) They even bought and sold, etc. - the AR and the GRA doubt this, since it is permissible since later they just bought from all the bloods, the sanctity of all the buying and later it is forbidden when they sold and left:",
    "5:ה": "(5) (ה) But if we did not give, etc. - the reason at that time when we bought, the sanctity applies to everything we bought and is not useful after the condition at the time of sale:",
