    "5:ז": "(7) (ז) And it is forbidden to change them only etc. And we built it in the High Court, but when we collected the tax from the people of the city, surely Dassor changed it, they didn't even pray anything there yet, and also if there is still the tax collection or trees and stones that they bought from them and as the author and the rabbi ruled. And the 11th reason for a dakbar came to the gabbai, and the MA wrote the reason for the fact that the tax was collected from the citizens of the city for the purpose of the High Court, it is blasphemous later if it is changed to lower the sanctity:",
    "5:ח": "(8) (ח) And if they brought trees, etc. - per the interpretation of the MA Meiri here, they did not go to collect them from the people of the city of Deza, not a bunch of them from Megbo Ma'at, but many were found who volunteered themselves and brought them, then it is permissible to change them before they came near Gabbai, and refer to the Bahl DH in Mashnin:",
