    "3:_": "And if the 17th rabbi ruled that excuses for the rabbi came near Gabbai, there is a sanctity for those deformities and it is forbidden to take them down, Efi will later give others, and even before they came near gabai, one should observe a vow of M. and the 16th difficulty for what purpose did Rabbi Davnim write 20 Dakhsh he is from mischief. To the tax collector, this time, he collects his money and they come to the tax collector. And here YL Dlau 29 is a DL Ma'at as an Arig Demi KMS the Tos' Sanhedrin MH A. D. Ha Momot and S. A invitation because the island came to the collector of Malta is an Mashak of stones griei Dakhtvi to Arig Demi Demush building and no invitation at all Hoi and Ima even came to the collector there is no holiness applicable to them KML and MSH DKAL from Megila 27 A. H. P. Duff per the method of the 16th Didi, a vow did not come out as a 1911 when they came to a collector, one needs a condition on what is permitted, and so what is frich Delma Rabbi Meiri did not come to a collector, they only collected it among themselves and did not hand over to the collector the deed of the deformity. The Rabbi even came to the collector of the permitted sub-collector from Dela Moki, as well as in their permits as 33 and Moki specifically in his sale as 11 and also means that the tax is equal to the body of the fund and in the permitted Mahani condition Shm Damiri in his sale 20, except that Shm Dain brings up the rule of what came to the collector and A'er Aut 8 and Mash A's and this son and IA in the MA will further:",
