    "15:ט": "(9) (ט) There is a difference between holy things and mitzvah things, which the RL Mitzvah will throw away after the mitzvah of Esi' 21. And sacred objects need to be ganizad in the preserved place (and in the KND, siman 4, they can, etc., not an obligation, rather, YAS) also, Ha Dayin Moridan from severity to lightness in sanctity. Hoi and APA Bhich will take an ark and it is forbidden to take it down, and we are not allowed to take it down and anything that is sacred inside it has an AMA letter 28 and APA it is forbidden to make a chair out of benches to sit in it, it is a sacred instrument, it has it and it is forbidden to take it down, even in a holy place, a fixed Hada for the Arai Kbasi KnD SO from an ark a chair. But from a little more to Aarai, see the answer of Rabbi Padvah Siman PB AMA KD Letter 13:",
